{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "nautobot",
  "description": "A Nautobot 2.x estate with three DCIM devices and one virtual machine. Payload keys and nesting follow a real depth=1 capture from demo.nautobot.com published as a test fixture by the gonautobot client, with synthetic identifiers and RFC 5737 addressing substituted. Proves the four things that distinguish Nautobot from NetBox and from a naive DRF client: status and role are related objects carrying a name rather than {value,label} choice dicts; interface type IS a {value,label} choice dict and a 'virtual' one is pooled rather than emitted as a second endpoint; device_type.manufacturer collapses to an {id,object_type,url} triple at depth=1 and so has to be joined from the manufacturers table; and software_version names its field 'version', not 'name'. Also proves the primary IP rides on the first physical interface, that an ip-only device still gets an interface, and that a disabled interface is skipped.",
